Done. All `server` package tests pass, including the two projector-related ones.

**Root cause:** In `server/create.go`, `ggufLayersWithMediaType` classified a GGUF as a projector layer only when `general.type` was `"projector"`. Published mmproj GGUFs (e.g. Gemma 4 VL, Qwen3-VL, LFM2-VL — see `convert/convert_gemma4.go`, `convert/convert_qwen3vl.go`) use `general.type = "mmproj"`, and when the vision block count is 0 they fell through to the default `application/vnd.ollama.image.model` media type.

**Fix** (`server/create.go`, `ggufLayersWithMediaType`):

```go
} else if (f.KV().Uint("block_count") == 0 && f.KV().Uint("vision.block_count") > 0) ||
    f.KV().Kind() == "projector" || f.KV().Kind() == "mmproj" {
    // if a model has vision.block_count but not block_count, it is a standalone vision model
    mediaType = "application/vnd.ollama.image.projector"
}
```

**Verification:**
- `go test ./server/...` — all pass
- `TestGGUFLayersClassifiesMMProjAsProjector` — PASS (mmproj GGUF now gets `application/vnd.ollama.image.projector`)
- `TestCreateModelAddsDefaultLlavaProjectorType` — PASS
